  "moduleTitle_GlacierModuleProperties": "Ice Chunk Module",
  "moduleDesc_GlacierModuleProperties": "Configures the zombies hidden inside Ice Chunks created by the Frostbite Caves Zomboss",
  "glacierModuleTitle": "Ice Chunk module",
  "glacierModuleHelpTitle": "Ice Chunk module",
  "glacierModuleHelpOverviewBody": "The Frostbite Caves Zomboss summons zombies differently from other Zomboss mechs: it spits out blasts of ice from bottom to top to create Ice Chunks, which release the zombies hidden inside when they break. This module is used to configure which zombies may appear inside the Ice Chunks.",
  "glacierModuleHelpColumnsTitle": "Parameters",
  "glacierModuleHelpColumnsBody": "This module consists of 6 content groups, with each group corresponding to one column of Ice Chunks. Counting starts from the column farthest from Zomboss, which is the leftmost column on a standard lawn. After selecting Add content, you can add either a zombie or the empty outcome \"No zombie appears.\" Every item has its own appearance weight; only zombie items can switch zombie type and set a level of up to Level 4, while the empty outcome only has a weight.",
  "glacierModuleHelpRequirementsTitle": "Notes",
  "glacierModuleHelpRequirementsBody": "This module must be used together with the Zomboss Mech Battle module, and the selected base Zomboss mech must be \"Frostbite Caves Zomboss (Zombot Tuskmaster 10,000 BC)\"; otherwise, it will have no effect.\nIn addition, using the Frostbite Caves Zomboss and the Ice Chunk Module on an Underwater World lawn is not recommended, as it negatively affects the overall appearance of the level.",
  "glacierModuleHelpPresetsTitle": "Preset configurations",
  "glacierModuleHelpPresetsBody": "The editor includes the Ice Chunk configurations used by each Frostbite Caves Zomboss variation in the original game. Applying a preset replaces all six Ice Chunk groups and cannot be undone; you can still adjust the entries manually afterward. The Beplanted variation does not need the Ice Chunk Module and therefore has no preset. The custom variation uses a blank preset by default.",
  "glacierModulePresetSectionTitle": "Ice Chunk presets",
  "glacierModulePresetBlankCustom": "Custom variation (blank preset)",
  "glacierModulePresetCustomConfiguration": "Custom configuration",
  "glacierModuleSwitchPresetTitle": "Switch Ice Chunk preset",
  "glacierModuleSwitchPresetMessage": "Switch from \"{from}\" to \"{to}\"? All six current Ice Chunk groups will be replaced and this cannot be undone.",
  "@glacierModuleSwitchPresetMessage": {"placeholders": {"from": {"type": "String"}, "to": {"type": "String"}}},
  "glacierModuleVariationPresetPromptTitle": "Enable the matching Ice Chunk preset",
  "glacierModuleVariationPresetPrompt": "The Frostbite Caves Zomboss summons zombies by filling Ice Chunks. The zombies released from those chunks are configured by the dedicated Ice Chunk Module. You are about to switch to another Frostbite Caves Zomboss variation. Also enable the Ice Chunk Module preset used by that variation in the original game?",
  "glacierModuleCustomVariationPresetPrompt": "The custom variation uses a blank Ice Chunk preset by default. Also switch the Ice Chunk Module to the blank preset?",
  "zombossMechSwitchVariationOnly": "Switch variation only",
  "glacierModuleEnablePreset": "Enable preset too",
  "iceAgePlantPuzzleVariationWarningTitle": "Beplanted does not need Ice Chunks",
  "iceAgePlantPuzzleVariationWarning": "The Beplanted variant of Zombot Tuskmaster 10,000 BC was designed specifically for the Beplanted minigame in Frostbite Caves. Its abilities do not require the Ice Chunk Module.",
  "glacierModuleCompatibilityWarningTitle": "Ice Chunk Module requirements",
  "glacierModuleCompatibilityWarning": "Ice Chunk Module must be used together with the Zomboss Mech Battle module, and the selected base Zomboss mech must be \"Frostbite Caves Zomboss (Zombot Tuskmaster 10,000 BC)\"; otherwise, it will have no effect. If you do not intend to use the Frostbite Caves Zomboss in this level, it is recommended to remove this module.",
