  "eventTitle_SpawnRocketLandingWaveActionProps": "Rocket Landing",
  "eventDesc_SpawnRocketLandingWaveActionProps": "Spawns capturable Moon rockets at set positions",
  "moonLifeSupportHelpTitle": "Life Support System",
  "moonLifeSupportHelpOverview": "An economy system commonly used in Moon BaseZ levels. After this module is added, planting does not cost Sun. Instead, plants occupy a portion of the Life Support System's power capacity in real time. When a plant is shoveled, destroyed by zombies, or removed by a special mechanic, all capacity it occupied is immediately restored.\nNote that this module also prevents Level 4 and higher plants from automatically using their Plant Food ability when planted.",
  "moonLifeSupportHelpProtocolsTitle": "Overload protocols",
  "moonLifeSupportHelpProtocols": "When the Life Support System's power usage exceeds its initial power capacity, the system enters an overloaded state and activates the Power-Saving Protocol, reducing the attack speed of plants on the lawn and the recharge speed of seed slots.\nWhen power usage exceeds (initial power capacity × required hibernation ratio), the system forcibly activates the Hibernation Protocol after the configured countdown, putting every plant on the lawn into hibernation. Seed slots and the Cosmic Plant Food meter are also locked and cannot be used.",
  "moonLifeSupportHelpPlantFoodTitle": "Independent cooldowns",
  "moonLifeSupportHelpPlantFood": "The module defines a dedicated list of plants with independent cooldowns. The cooldowns of plants in this list are not affected by the Power-Saving Protocol, but those plants still cannot be planted under the Hibernation Protocol.",
  "moonLifeSupportPowerSettings": "Power settings",
  "moonInitialCapacity": "Initial power capacity (InitialCapacity)",
  "moonBufferOverloadRatio": "Required hibernation ratio (BufferOverloadRatio)",
  "moonPenaltyCountdown": "Hibernation countdown (PenaltyCountdown, seconds)",
  "moonPlantImmunityList": "Plants with independent cooldowns (PlantImmunityList)",
  "moonPlantImmunityListHint": "The cooldowns of plants in this list are not affected by the Power-Saving Protocol, but those plants still cannot be planted under the Hibernation Protocol.",
  "moonSelectImmunePlants": "Select plants to add to the list",
  "lunarTerminalHelpTitle": "Lunar Terminal",
  "lunarTerminalHelpOverview": "An Artifact commonly used in Moon BaseZ levels. It remains at a fixed position on the lawn, similar to the cannon in Sky City. After tapping the collection terminal, select one of three mining robots and drag it onto the lawn. Robots automatically collect energy from Lunar Energy Crystals and Radioactive Meteorites within range, permanently increasing the base Life Support System's available power capacity for the current level and allowing stronger lineups. Robots have health and can be attacked and destroyed by zombies, Radioactive Meteorites, and other targets.",
  "lunarTerminalHelpFixedTitle": "Deployment cooldown",
  "lunarTerminalHelpFixed": "After deploying a robot, the Lunar Energy Collection Terminal enters a cooldown period. The cooldown duration can be customized in the level.",
  "lunarTerminalCollectorCooldown": "Robot deployment cooldown (CollectorCooldown, seconds)",
  "lunarMineVeinHelpTitle": "Crystal Veins",
  "lunarMineVeinHelpOverview": "Places Lunar Energy Crystal Veins on the lawn at the start of the level, as commonly seen in Moon Base. Veins initially provide no energy. Once the configured wave begins, a crystal of the corresponding type grows at the same position and can be mined according to its properties. Select a vein type, then tap a grid cell to place it. Right-click on desktop or long-press on mobile to remove it.",
  "lunarMineVeinTypePalette": "Crystal vein type",
  "lunarMineVeinHelpHardened": "Protected by a sturdy outer layer of rock. The shell must first be destroyed by plant attacks before the crystal can be mined normally. Hard-Shell Crystal Veins always grow the 3,000 HP version of the Hard-Shell Crystal.",
  "lunarMineVeinHelpFragile": "Mining continuously consumes its durability until the crystal shatters. Special Fragile Crystal Veins containing Cosmic Plant Food can also be placed.",
  "lunarMineVeinHelpRadiation": "Periodically releases radiation in all directions. Plants exposed to the radiation will randomly transform into other plants, while irradiated zombies will either take damage or mutate into a Cosmic Radiation Gargantuar. Cosmic Radiation Gargantuars have extremely high health and will also irradiate nearby plants and zombies when defeated.",
  "lunarMineVeinHelpWaveTitle": "Wave numbering",
  "lunarMineVeinHelpWave": "Growth wave (EmergenceWave) is numbered from 1. Enter 1 to grow on the first wave, 2 to grow on the second wave, and so on.",
  "lunarMineVeinPlacements": "Vein placements (VeinPlacements)",
  "lunarMineVeinModuleExpectationLabel": "Crystal Veins",
  "lunarMineVeinModulePreviewEmerging": "Lunar Energy Crystals emerging this wave:",
  "lunarMineEmergenceWave": "Growth wave (EmergenceWave, 1-based)",
  "moonPlacementGestureHint": "Tap an empty tile to add an entry. Right-click or long-press an occupied tile to remove it.",
